# Intro
A uniform, periodic box of 1000 H nuclei per cm^3 at 100 K, with no star and no light, run
with geajay cooling and the ISRF switched on. H2 forms on dust and through H-, and nothing
else acts. The box therefore has an exact answer: the rate at which the H2 abundance
`x2 = n_H2 / n_H` grows follows from the gas state alone, through the formation coefficients
of the published chemistry fits. The check compares the measured growth of every gas particle
with that rate. It tests the size and the sign of each formation channel, which a comparison
of two runs of the same code cannot do.

Two arms isolate the two channels:

| Arm | Metallicity | `n_HII / n_H` | Channel that forms H2 |
|---|---|---|---|
| `hminus` | 0 | 1e-5 | H- only: `HI + e- -> H-`, then `H- + HI -> H2 + e-` |
| `dust` | 0.1 solar | 1e-8 | dust grains only |

Both arms start at `x2 = 1e-8`. In the H- arm `x2` grows by 1.6e-6 in 0.05 Myr, in the dust arm
by 5e-3.

`with_radiative_cooling: 0` keeps the internal energy of the gas fixed while the chemistry
runs, so the temperature stays at 100 K, apart from the change of the mean molecular weight.

# Configure
```
./configure --with-chemistry=GEAR_10 --with-feedback=GEAR --with-cooling=geajay_3 --with-stars=GEAR --with-sink=GEAR --with-star-formation=GEAR --with-tracers=GEAR --with-kernel=wendland-C2 --with-geajay=path/to/geajay --with-chealpix=path/to/chealpix
make -j
```
The geajay library must have no default for the far-UV field G_0 (SWIFT stops at start-up
otherwise) and must provide `with_radiative_cooling`. The ISRF reads the radiation table
`PopII_parsec_spectral.hdf5`, which `run.sh` fetches. The box has no star, so the table
only has to load.

# Run
```
arm=dust ./run.sh
arm=hminus ./run.sh
```
Each run takes about 10 s on 4 threads: 4096 gas particles (level 4), 0.05 Myr, one snapshot
every 0.005 Myr. `run.sh` writes the snapshots, `used_parameters.yml` and `timesteps.txt` into
a directory named after the arm (`run_name` changes it). `extra="-P Key:value"` passes more
swift parameters. `run.sh` stops if `snap/` or the run directory exists (`force=1` removes
them). `level`, `gas_density` (atom/cm^3, `n_H` is 0.76 times it) and `gas_mass` (Msun) set the
box.

# Checking
```
python3 check_h2_formation_rates.py --arm dust dust/snap
python3 check_h2_formation_rates.py --arm hminus hminus/snap
```
For each snapshot interval the check forms the median over particles of
`ln(measured rate / reference rate)`. The reference is the trapezoid mean of the formation rate
of the two snapshot states: dust grains (Omukai 2000, with the grain temperature solved from
the grain energy balance), H- with the H- abundance in steady state, H2+ and three-body
formation. The bar of each interval is the sum of the numerical terms listed in the script
docstring: the trapezoid rule, the H- relaxation, float32 storage, the temperature and the
solver tolerance. The species of a snapshot hold the state of the last step that ended before
its time, so the check takes the elapsed time from `timesteps.txt`. The first interval starts
from the start-up state and is printed but not gated.

Exit status: 0 pass, 1 a failed bar (also a particle with no positive growth), 2 a missing
file, 3 a value that is not finite, 4 a run that does not meet the premises of the check (a star
or light in the box, a solver other than 1, a temperature that moved).

`--expected-dust-to-gas` gives the reference dust-to-gas ratio of the model (default 0.009387,
the library value). `extra="-P GeajayCooling:reference_dust_to_gas_ratio:0.018774"` runs a
box with twice that ratio; it fails the default check and passes with
`--expected-dust-to-gas 0.018774`. `--plant-formation-scale S` multiplies the H2 growth by S,
and `--plant-hm-sign` mirrors it, as a flipped H- term would. `--plant-nan` puts a NaN in the
last snapshot. These options plant a known error in the data read from the snapshots, to
confirm that the check fails when it should.

The check does not see errors that appear only in the light (H- photodetachment, the dust
temperature in a transported field), a wrong `k8` (H- turns into H2 with a share of 0.999 in
the H- arm), or three-body formation (it needs `n_H` above 1e8 cm^-3).
